exports[`snapshots: every lifecycle email, text and HTML > tip next: quarantine to reject > text 1`] = `
"Hi Dana,

For the last two weeks (2–15 Nov, UTC), every message in brightwave-mail.com's reports passed DMARC: 2,480 messages from 3 sources.

100% of 2,480 reported messages passed DMARC in the last 14 days, so your senders look ready. brightwave-mail.com's own DMARC record sets p=quarantine, so mail from brightwave-mail.com that fails DMARC is quarantined, usually to spam.

The record this change publishes, at _dmarc.brightwave-mail.com:

    v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:rua@rua.readysetmail.com

Mail that passes DMARC is not affected by this change.

Moving to p=reject is done in stages; the domain page shows each step when the reports support it.

Open brightwave-mail.com: https://app.example.test/#/w/ws_brightwave/domains/7

Why am I getting this? You are the owner of Brightwave Studio on Ready Set Mail, and you turned on tips about your domains.

Turn off tips about your domains: https://app.example.test/api/email-preferences/off?t=TOKEN
Email settings: https://app.example.test/#/w/ws_brightwave/settings"
`;
